   "subject": "Sigmoidal regression formula in INLA",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(79,79,79)\">Hi All,</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(79,79,79)\">I want to make a sigmodial regression <span style=\"line-height:18px\">(i.e., a logistic without the 0 to 1 limit)</span><span style=\"line-height:18px\"> in INLA with a negative binomial or quasipoisson distribution</span><span style=\"line-height:18px\">, as the one specified below in BUGS language. I don&#39;t know how to specify such a model, if possible, in the formula required by INLA. </span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"><span style=\"line-height:18px\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"><span style=\"line-height:18px\">Any help would be much appreciated.</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"><span style=\"line-height:18px\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"><span style=\"line-height:18px\">Ignacio</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(79,79,79)\"># Sigmodal regression y ~ b_0 / (1 + exp(b_1 + b_2*x[i]))</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0);min-height:17px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">model {</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0);min-height:17px\">      </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">  # priors</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">  b_0 ~ dnorm(0, 0.001)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">  b_1 ~ dnorm(0, 0.001)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">  b_2 ~ dnorm(0, 0.001)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0);min-height:17px\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\">  </span><span style=\"line-height:18px\">alpha &lt;- exp(lalpha)</span><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">  lalpha ~ dnorm(0,0001)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0);min-height:17px\">       <span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">  # likelihood</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">  for (i in 1:N.po)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>{</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">    y[i] ~ dpois(must[i])</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">    must[i] &lt;- rho[i] * lambda[i]</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">    rho[i] ~ dgamma(alpha, alpha)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">    log(lambda[i]) &lt;- b_0 / (1 + exp(z[i]))</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">    z[i] &lt;- b_1 + b_2*x[i]<span style=\"line-height:18px\">        </span><span style=\"line-height:18px;white-space:pre\">\t</span><span style=\"line-height:18px\"> </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">  } </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\">}</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal;font-family:Monaco;color:rgb(176,22,0)\"><br></p><div><span style=\"color:#061a99\"><br></span></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
